## 2. Architecture

Layering follows the established convention: `infrastructure/*` holds
`@Global()` technical capabilities behind DI-token abstractions; `features/*`
holds controllers + services serving both external callers and in-process
principals (`SYSTEM_PRINCIPAL`).

```
                external users                 agents / pipeline / modules
                      │                                     │
                      ▼                                     ▼
          POST /search/:index                    SearchService (internal API)
              (SearchController)          ┌───────────────┴───────────────┐
                      │                   │                               │
                      └──────────►  SearchService  ◄── enqueueIndex/Delete/reindex
                                          │                               │
                    owner-scope filter    │                    ┌──────────▼──────────┐
                    injection (server)    │                    │  search-indexing    │
                                          │                    │  BullMQ queue       │
                                          ▼                    └──────────┬──────────┘
                                   SEARCH_ENGINE  ◄─── worker applies ─────┘
                                  (infrastructure)         + waitForTask
                                          │
                                          ▼
                                    MeiliSearch (local)
```

### 2.1 Module layout

```
src/infrastructure/search-engine/
  search-engine.module.ts            # @Global; provides MEILI_CLIENT + SEARCH_ENGINE
  meili.constants.ts                 # DI tokens (symbols) + type aliases
  meili.provider.ts                  # builds MeiliSearch client from validated config
  search-engine.interface.ts         # SearchEngine abstraction + supporting types
  search-engine.service.ts           # MeiliSearch-backed, index-agnostic impl

src/config/configurations/
  search.config.ts                   # registerAs('search', …)   (+ env.validation.ts, config.module.ts)

src/infrastructure/health/
  meili.health.ts                    # Terminus indicator (mirrors minio.health.ts; wired into health.module.ts)

src/features/search-service/
  search-service.module.ts
  search.controller.ts               # external HTTP API (POST /search/:index)
  search.service.ts                  # internal API + used by controller
  index-registry.ts                  # index definitions (name, primaryKey, settings, ownerScope)
  search.types.ts                    # request/response types, IndexName, access-scope types
  search.constants.ts                # queue name, job names, DI tokens
  processors/search-indexing.processor.ts       # BullMQ worker (idempotent apply)
  schedulers/search-reconciliation.scheduler.ts # periodic drift repair / reindex trigger
  dto/search-query.dto.ts            # Zod schema for the external search request

src/common/                          # promoted shared utilities (see §10)
  principal.ts                       # Principal + SYSTEM_PRINCIPAL
  decorators/current-user.decorator.ts
  pipes/zod-validation.pipe.ts
```

### 2.2 Dependency & registration

- `SearchEngineModule` is `@Global()` (like `FileManageModule`) so any feature
  can inject `SEARCH_ENGINE` without importing it.
- `SearchServiceModule` registers the `search-indexing` BullMQ queue
  (`BullModule.registerQueue`), the controller, service, processor, scheduler,
  and the index registry provider.
- `AppModule` import order: add `SearchEngineModule` in the infrastructure
  block (after `FileManageModule`), and `SearchServiceModule` in the feature
  block. **Mastra stays last** (its catch-all controller must not shadow routes).
- `MeiliHealthIndicator` is added to `HealthModule` alongside the MinIO one.

