## 3. Configuration

New `search` config namespace, validated in the single Zod env schema
(`env.validation.ts`) and exposed via `registerAs('search', …)`, consumed by the
provider, health indicator, and feature.

The three connection variables below already exist in `.env`
(`MEILISEARCH_HOST`, `MEILISEARCH_PORT`, `MEILISEARCH_MASTER_KEY`); the rest are
new and follow the same `MEILISEARCH_`/`SEARCH_` naming. The master key is a
secret — it is read from env only and never logged, returned, or committed.

| Env var | Type / default | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `MEILISEARCH_HOST` | string, `localhost` | Meili host (**existing**) |
| `MEILISEARCH_PORT` | int, `30770` | Meili port (**existing**) |
| `MEILISEARCH_MASTER_KEY` | string (required in prod) | admin key used server-side (**existing**) |
| `MEILISEARCH_USE_SSL` | bool, `false` | http vs https when composing the URL (new) |
| `MEILISEARCH_INDEX_PREFIX` | string, `''` | optional namespace prefix for index names (env isolation) (new) |
| `MEILISEARCH_TASK_TIMEOUT_MS` | int, `10000` | max wait for a Meili async task in the worker (new) |
| `MEILISEARCH_SEARCH_TIMEOUT_MS` | int, `5000` | client request timeout for search (new) |
| `SEARCH_DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE` | int, `20` | default `limit` (new) |
| `SEARCH_MAX_PAGE_SIZE` | int, `100` | hard cap on `limit` (new) |

`search.config.ts` composes the client URL (`http(s)://host:port`) and exposes a
typed `SearchConfig`. A `superRefine` (matching the existing MinIO rule) rejects
an empty `MEILISEARCH_MASTER_KEY` when `NODE_ENV=production`.

