## 4. Infrastructure — `SEARCH_ENGINE` provider

Two DI tokens, mirroring `MINIO_CLIENT` / `OBJECT_STORAGE`:

```ts
// meili.constants.ts
export const MEILI_CLIENT = Symbol('MEILI_CLIENT');    // raw client (health + advanced)
export const SEARCH_ENGINE = Symbol('SEARCH_ENGINE');  // index-agnostic abstraction
```

`meili.provider.ts` builds the client from config (stateless HTTP client, so —
like MinIO — no shutdown lifecycle needed):

```ts
new MeiliSearch({ host, apiKey, timeout: searchTimeoutMs });
```

### 4.1 The `SearchEngine` abstraction (illustrative)

Index-agnostic; knows nothing about files or any domain. All mutating ops return
a task reference so callers (the worker) can await consistency off the hot path.

```ts
export interface IndexDefinition {
  name: string;
  primaryKey: string;
  searchableAttributes: string[];
  filterableAttributes: string[];
  sortableAttributes: string[];
  rankingRules?: string[];
  settings?: Partial<MeiliIndexSettings>;   // faceting, typoTolerance, pagination.maxTotalHits, etc.
}

export interface EngineQuery {
  q: string;
  filter?: string | string[];   // built server-side ONLY (never raw user input — §7)
  sort?: string[];
  facets?: string[];
  page?: number;                // 1-based; maps to Meili page/hitsPerPage
  hitsPerPage?: number;
  attributesToRetrieve?: string[];
  attributesToHighlight?: string[];
  attributesToCrop?: string[];
}

export interface EngineResult<T> {
  hits: T[];
  totalHits: number;
  page: number;
  hitsPerPage: number;
  totalPages: number;
  facetDistribution?: Record<string, Record<string, number>>;
  processingTimeMs: number;
}

export interface TaskRef { taskUid: number; }

export interface SearchEngine {
  ensureIndex(def: IndexDefinition): Promise<void>;            // create if absent + updateSettings (idempotent)
  addOrReplace<T>(index: string, docs: T[]): Promise<TaskRef>;
  update<T>(index: string, docs: Array<Partial<T>>): Promise<TaskRef>;
  deleteDocuments(index: string, ids: string[]): Promise<TaskRef>;
  deleteByFilter(index: string, filter: string | string[]): Promise<TaskRef>;
  clearIndex(index: string): Promise<TaskRef>;
  search<T>(index: string, query: EngineQuery): Promise<EngineResult<T>>;
  multiSearch<T>(queries: Array<{ index: string } & EngineQuery>): Promise<Array<EngineResult<T>>>;
  waitForTask(taskUid: number): Promise<'succeeded' | 'failed' | 'canceled'>;
  generateTenantToken(searchRules: unknown, opts?: { expiresAt?: Date }): string; // capability; unused now
  health(): Promise<boolean>;
}
```

### 4.2 `SearchEngineService` responsibilities

- Translate the abstraction into `meilisearch` SDK calls against
  `client.index(prefix + name)`.
- Apply `MEILISEARCH_INDEX_PREFIX` centrally so callers use bare index names.
- `ensureIndex`: `getIndex`-or-`createIndex`, then `updateSettings` — safe to run
  on every boot; converges settings.
- Map `page`/`hitsPerPage` to Meili's exhaustive pagination (returns
  `totalHits`/`totalPages`), honoring the per-index `pagination.maxTotalHits`.
- `waitForTask` polls `client.tasks.waitForTask(uid, { timeOutMs })`; on `failed`
  it reads the task error and throws a typed `SearchEngineError`.
- Never accept a raw Meili filter string from outside its callers — filters are
  composed from typed inputs by the feature layer.

### 4.3 Health indicator

`MeiliHealthIndicator` mirrors `MinioHealthIndicator`: calls `client.health()`
(or `isHealthy()`), returns Terminus `up()`/`down()`. Registered in
`HealthModule` and surfaced by the existing health controller.

