## 5. Feature — `search-service`

### 5.1 Index registry

Central declaration of every index, its Meili settings, and its access rule.
Consumers add a definition here (files later). At `OnApplicationBootstrap`, the
service calls `SEARCH_ENGINE.ensureIndex(def)` for each registered index so
settings are converged at startup.

```ts
export interface RegisteredIndex extends IndexDefinition {
  ownerScope?: { attribute: string; allowPublic?: boolean }; // e.g. { attribute: 'ownerId', allowPublic: true }
  allowedFilterFields: string[];    // whitelist projected onto filterableAttributes
  allowedSortFields: string[];      // whitelist projected onto sortableAttributes
}
```

`IndexName` is a union/enum of registered names; the controller/service reject
unknown indexes with `404`/`400` before touching Meili.

### 5.2 Internal `SearchService` API (agents / pipeline / modules)

```ts
class SearchService {
  // indexing (async, idempotent — enqueues BullMQ jobs, returns immediately)
  enqueueIndex(index: IndexName, docs: object[]): Promise<void>;
  enqueueDelete(index: IndexName, ids: string[]): Promise<void>;
  reindex(index: IndexName): Promise<void>;   // enqueues a full rebuild job

  // querying (synchronous)
  search<T>(index: IndexName, request: SearchRequest, principal: Principal): Promise<SearchResults<T>>;
}
```

Internal callers use `SYSTEM_PRINCIPAL` and therefore search **unscoped** (see
§7). This is the surface agents and other modules depend on.

### 5.3 External `SearchController`

```
POST /search/:index          # body: SearchRequest (Zod-validated); index path param validated against registry
```

- Resolves the acting `Principal` via `@CurrentUser()` (placeholder today; real
  auth guard binds later — same pattern as `FileController`).
- Delegates to `SearchService.search(index, body, principal)`.
- Non-system principals are **owner-scoped server-side** (§7); a user cannot
  broaden the scope.
- (Design allows a later `POST /search` multi-index/federated endpoint via
  `multiSearch`; not built now.)

### 5.4 Request / response contract

`SearchRequest` (Zod DTO):

```ts
{
  q: string;                                    // '' allowed → returns by ranking/sort
  page?: number;             // 1-based, default 1
  limit?: number;            // default SEARCH_DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE, capped at SEARCH_MAX_PAGE_SIZE
  filters?: Record<string, string | number | boolean | Array<string | number>>;  // field → value(s), allowlisted
  sort?: string[];           // "field:asc" | "field:desc", allowlisted
  facets?: string[];         // allowlisted
  highlight?: string[];      // subset of searchable attributes
}
```

`SearchResults<T>`:

```ts
{
  hits: T[];
  page: number;
  limit: number;
  totalHits: number;
  totalPages: number;
  facetDistribution?: Record<string, Record<string, number>>;
  processingTimeMs: number;
}
```

The service converts the structured `filters`/`sort` into a validated Meili
filter/sort expression (see §7.2) — clients never send raw Meili syntax.

